niversity-physics-volume-2","subject":"Science","subjects":[{"id":264,"meta":{"type":"books.BookSubjects"},"subject_name":"Science","subject_page_content":"Simple to use, simple to adopt. Our science textbooks are designed to meet the standard scope and sequence requirements of their respective courses – and are 100% free online. Complete with free resources for educators (like LMS course shells, lecture slides, instructor answer keys, and more), all OpenStax textbooks are fully customizable. Explore our texts below and adopt any and all parts useful to your course.","subject_search_description":"Science"}],"theme":"green"},"page":{"abstract":"\u003cp xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xmlns:epub=\"http://www.idpf.org/2007/ops\" xmlns:m=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" id=\"para-00001\">By the end of this section, you will be able to:\u003c/p>\u003cul xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xmlns:epub=\"http://www.idpf.org/2007/ops\" xmlns:m=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" id=\"list-00001\">\n\u003cli>Use Lenz’s law to determine the direction of induced emf whenever a magnetic flux changes\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use Faraday’s law with Lenz’s law to determine the induced emf in a coil and in a solenoid\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>","id":"64d72376-ecca-4e42-b51e-07c2757ed8dc","title":"Lenz's Law","noindex":false}},"errors":{"sentryMessageIdStack":[],"showDialog":false,"code":200},"featureFlags":{},"head":{"links":[{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-2-lenzs-law"}],"meta":[{"name":"description","content":"The direction in which the induced emf drives current around a wire loop can be found through the negative sign. However, it is usually easier to determ..."},{"property":"og:description","content":"The direction in which the induced emf drives current around a wire loop can be found through the negative sign. However, it is usually easier to determ..."},{"property":"og:title","content":"13.2 Lenz's Law - Uni